source: src/main.rs
expression: sub.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Publish one session's transcript to a public link.

Renders the session as a self-contained HTML page and writes it to the `[share]` bucket (or `--to` for an ad-hoc destination), then prints the public URL. No redaction is applied - anything in the transcript, including secrets, becomes public. Requires `--yes` or an interactive confirm.

Usage: pond share [OPTIONS] <SESSION_ID>

Arguments:
  <SESSION_ID>
          The session to publish

Options:
      --to <URL>
          Ad-hoc publish destination, overriding `[share].bucket`. Same URL grammar and `[creds.*]` resolution as any other storage address

      --viewer <VIEWER>
          Overrides `[share].viewer` for this run
          
          [possible values: html]

      --yes
          Skip the interactive confirm prompt

      --open
          Open the published URL in the default browser after publishing

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --storage-path <URL>
          Storage destination: a local path or remote URL.
          
          Accepts a bare path, `~/path`, `file://`, `s3://bucket/prefix`, `s3+https://host/bucket/prefix`, `gs://`, `az://`, or the keyword `local` (the platform default local data dir). Default: `[storage].path` from config, then the platform data dir (`~/.local/share/pond`).
          
          [env: POND_STORAGE_PATH]

      --config-file <PATH>
          Config file to read (default: `~/.config/pond/config.toml`)
          
          [env: POND_CONFIG_FILE]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

Examples:
  pond share 01HXY...                            confirm interactively, publish to [share].bucket
  pond share 01HXY... --yes                      skip the confirm prompt
  pond share 01HXY... --to s3://bucket/shares    publish to an ad-hoc bucket
  pond share 01HXY... --yes --open               publish and open the URL in a browser
